he's the ruler of dubai but stands  accused of breaking british law the high  court ruling sheikh muhammad al maktoum  ordered the phones of his ex-wife and  her lawyers to be hacked in an ongoing  custody battle taking place in the uk  it found princess heyer and her  barrister the conservative peer baroness  shackleton had their phones targeted by  multi-million pound spyware called  pegasus a program manufactured by an  israeli company the nso group and sold  exclusively to nation states  usually i'm used to investigating  surveillance against journalists and  dissidents this is kind of the first  time that i saw uh or you know what i  thought was basically government spyware  being used  potentially against someone's ex-wife  and their lawyers in a child custody  case  the hacking came to light via a chain of  connections involving sherry blair the  wife of former british prime minister  tony blair was an adviser to nso and  contacted baroness shackleton about the  potential surveillance after being told  the pegasus software may have been  misused  it can be used to take over a person's  entire device and that means that it can  pull all of the data off even encrypted  messaging  it can be used to covertly activate a  microphone a camera and the really  troubling thing is that you would  probably never know about it the case  being heard here on the surface is  intensely personal it's a divorce battle  over custody of two children but these  latest judgments stretch well beyond the  personal sphere described by the court  as being serial breaches of uk law and  an abuse of power to a significant  extent  sheikh mohammed who offered no evidence  to the court said i have always denied  the allegations made against me and i  continue to do so the findings were  based on evidence that was not disclosed  to me or my advisors i therefore  maintain that they were made in a manner  which was unfair  it's not the first time the sheikh has  been the focus of a damning ruling from  the high court last year it found the 72  year old orchestrated the abduction and  forced return to dubai of two of his  daughters sheikha latifah and sheikha  shamsa and now this close ally of  britain is facing further questions over  how far he attempts to exert his power  iva bennett sky news
 

